| !AArdvarkLoader: loads RISC OS on Linux's own modules at start-up (discs
| in RISC OS's format, sound, USB and the rest). It is an application in
| Choices:Boot.PreDesk so that a PreDesk file that fails can't leave them
| unloaded (the files there are run in order and the run stops at the first
| that fails; the applications are run afterwards all the same), and its
| name puts it first among them. The list of what is loaded is
| Choices:Boot.TestBed. Keep the name and the place.
|
| Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Youll. MIT licence (see LICENSE).
IconSprites <Obey$Dir>.!Sprites
If "<AArdvarkLoader$Loaded>" = "" Then IfThere Choices:Boot.TestBed Then Obey Choices:Boot.TestBed
Set AArdvarkLoader$Loaded 1
